+
+`IM_max >= Im_min = 1 + principal_minor_floor + other_minor_floor`.
+
+For a bottom major packet of f-mass `v*m/d_2`, the code's contribution to the upper bound is
+
+`(v*m/d_2) * n/(m+n) * (1-delta_1)`.
+
+Xu Theorem5.1 gives the sum over final major roots. Any further refinement has radius at least `delta_1`, so distributing the fixed mass among later final packets cannot increase this expression. Thus this is an upper bound; no omitted split is assumed attained. Nonzero A-orbits carry A conjugate packets and the recursion sums each distinct packet once.
+
+For an internal minor packet of multiplicity v, the code uses the first possible zero-order radius
+
+`rho_0 = delta_j + [d_j/(n-M_j)]*(1-delta_j)/v`
+
