+There is no further hidden parity or gcd condition. `Skel.u` at line 82 is `V_s K/d_s`, a **major** capacity, not the FS minor multiplicity `u_s=d_s-V_s`. It is computed, not tested. Confusing these quantities would corrupt a coverage statement; the operative code computes `u_s` separately. `delta_s=-1`, `delta_{s-1}>=0`, all lower tower radii `<1`, and increasing radii follow from the existing arithmetic and Def.5.1; omitting separate assertions does not omit their consequences. For example, `delta_{s-1}=[u_s(n-M_{s-1})-d_s]/[V_s(n-M_{s-1})-d_s]>=0`, since the positive difference `n-M_{s-1}` is divisible by `d_s` (Lemma6.1 p.194).
