+Core exhaustiveness is also a proof about loops, not an inference from those tests. Given a normalized realized row, its K and coprime reduced ratio occur in the outer loops; its strict gcd chain occurs in `divisor_chains`; its increasing M-values occur in every `Mrec` interval. Starting at the top, its actual multiplicity lies inside each integer V window and satisfies the two-point strict bound. Inductively R and LCM are exactly Def.5.1's product and upper denominator LCM. The all-degree orbit and terminal tests therefore retain that multiplicity. The generator yields the row. No step uses `n<=100` or `s<=5`.
+
+**The operative whole-tree screen.** The charged scope report's implementation is `scope_enum.operative -> opus5_probe.Tree`, with `gate=False`, `ode=True`, `recenter=True`, `capacity=False`, `passport=False`. An independent `full_tree_partition` implementation is used by the Xu driver. Both were replayed against **every one of the 24,063 rows**, with zero difference between their survivor sets, not merely equal totals.
+
+At an internal level j, the branch-specific quantities are
+
+`P=V_{j+1}d_j/d_{j+1}`, `Q=V_{j+1}(n-M_j)/d_{j+1}`, `lo=P/Q=d_j/(n-M_j)`.
+
+These are `deg p`, `deg q`, and the major threshold in Prop.4.6 p.170 / Prop.5.3 p.182. The operative P,Q are not the core's temporary variable named Q in `div9`.
